  "summary": "The Trump administration is reasserting its controversial stance on vaccine policy with a new order questioning the childhood immunization schedule, reversing recent efforts to avoid the politically fraught topic. Meanwhile, the FDA is pushing forward on food safety transparency by requiring manufacturers to disclose additives under the GRAS loophole, an action that aligns with RFK Jr.'s policy agenda. On the drug development front, several clinical programs have stumbled this week—including Sionna's cystic fibrosis pill, Tenax's heart failure drug, and an FDA rejection of a radiopharmaceutical therapy due to manufacturing concerns—highlighting persistent challenges even as radiopharmaceuticals remain an area of intense investor interest and biotech IPO activity. Health systems are increasingly grappling with AI deployment challenges, particularly around managing AI lifecycles, addressing evidence gaps in drug development, and preventing sophisticated AI-enabled fraud in home health, while simultaneously exploring AI applications for clinician burden reduction and early disease detection. Recent funding and partnership announcements in rural health innovation, AI drug discovery, and Medicare quality reporting suggest continued industry momentum in digital health infrastructure despite regulatory headwinds and clinical setbacks.",
